761d4050","cmd-9c3efd9d74844061","cmd-3bfe85f12faf4712","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The dedicated node2 uploader key successfully submits byte-exact batches to separate node1 receipts, while command execution, shells, and forwarding are denied. Seeded data, administrative policy, OS, kernel, security controls, and package state were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and a successful post-restart cross-node submission.","limitations":["Forwarding behavior was directly exercised for local TCP forwarding; denial of remote, agent, X11, and tunnel forwarding is established by the effective sshd policy rather than separate successful behavioral probes.","Administrative separation is directly shown by distinct accounts and node1's effective root SSH policy, but no live administrative SSH login was captured."]}
